{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_17_engineering_governance_laws", "label": "The Nine Laws (non-negotiable)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The repository \u2014 not any agent's memory \u2014 is the source of engineering truth, so the Laws live in one governance document that CLAUDE.md points to and the always-loaded rules file digests."}, {"id": "docs_17_engineering_governance_law_4", "label": "Law 4 \u2014 Single Source of Truth", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Duplicate definitions are defects, not conveniences: enums to contracts, visual values to generated tokens, schema to migrations, money formatting to formatInr, strings to the i18n catalog."}, {"id": "docs_17_engineering_governance_law_7", "label": "Law 7 \u2014 Cross-Platform Lockstep", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Platform drift is a violation, not a follow-up; exceptions require an explicit owner ruling because the default is lockstep verified in the browser AND on both simulators."}, {"id": "docs_17_engineering_governance_law_9", "label": "Law 9 \u2014 Incremental Schema & API Growth", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Big-bang schema implementation guarantees refactors and drift once real slices meet reality, so tables, enums, contracts and endpoints are authored only when their owning module's slice begins."}, {"id": "docs_17_engineering_governance_decision_hierarchy", "label": "Decision Hierarchy (9 levels + two tiebreakers)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never invent at level N what a higher level already defines; a per-package CLAUDE.md beats a cross-cutting rule because it is closer to the code, and a dated ADR beats a prose doc."}, {"id": "docs_17_engineering_governance_rule_mechanism_matrix", "label": "Rule \u2192 Mechanism Matrix (enforced / planned / prose)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A rule at stage 'prose' must say why no mechanism can hold it \u2014 that requirement is what stops prose quietly accumulating again. Notably, 'a fact both platforms need lives in a package' is enforced by nothing, because detecting it mechanically means comparing meaning, not text."}, {"id": "docs_17_engineering_governance_traceability", "label": "Traceability without a roadmap system (plans + .qa evidence)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-module roadmaps cost more to maintain than the traceability they bought and a stale roadmap actively misleads; status is never 'done' without evidence recording what was run, on what surface, and what was seen."}, {"id": "docs_17_engineering_governance_package_claudemd_template", "label": "Per-package CLAUDE.md template (landmines are mandatory)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Landmines do not count against the line budget: they are the healthiest part of the corpus and capping them would delete the incident record \u2014 an hour lost to a trap nobody wrote down is an hour the next person also loses."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_17_engineering_governance_laws", "target": "docs_17_engineering_governance_law_4", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_17_engineering_governance_laws", "target": "docs_17_engineering_governance_law_7", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_17_engineering_governance_laws", "target": "docs_17_engineering_governance_law_9", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_17_engineering_governance_law_9", "target": "docs_04_data_model_frozen_design", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_17_engineering_governance_law_9", "target": "docs_forward_compat_register", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_17_engineering_governance_law_4", "target": "docs_10_i18n_and_design_system_token_pipeline", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/17-engineering-governance.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_17_engineering_governance_law_4", "target": "docs_10_i18n_and_design_system_formatting_law", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/